# Git workflow

After completing a logical set of edits (feature, fix, or task):

1. Run `git status` and stage only the files that belong to the change.
2. Commit with a clear, conventional message (what changed and why).
3. Push the current branch to `origin` (e.g. `git push origin <branch>`).

Do not leave fixes uncommitted at the end of a session unless the user explicitly asks to hold commits.
